WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.741
Don't expect to hear this word&nbsp;
when you watch "Creed III."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.741 --> 00:00:08.734
Here's why Tessa Thompson absolutely&nbsp;
refused to say this word on camera.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:12.300
Tessa Thomposon isn't pulling any punches&nbsp;
when it comes to shaping her "Creed III"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.800
character. While Adonis Creed's journey on&nbsp;
the silver screen has largely been shaped by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.480
the guidance and training he's received from&nbsp;
Rocky Balboa, it's important to note just how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.160
important Bianca is to the boxing superstar.&nbsp;
A musician, Thompson's character was first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.312
introduced in 2015's "Creed," where she served&nbsp;
as Adonis' love interest and emotional rock.

00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:35.520
"Creed" wasn't just a one-off. A box&nbsp;
office juggernaut and Oscar nominee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.080
it went on to spawn a successful sequel&nbsp;
in 2018. Now, it's threequel time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.120
and Thompson's character is just as relevant&nbsp;
as she was on day one. With Bianca such a key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.960
part of the "Creed" mythology, Thompson&nbsp;
has made it clear just how important it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.700
is for her to shape Bianca. The actor said as&nbsp;
much in an exclusive interview with Looper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.266
where she opened up about being hands-on with&nbsp;
how the "Creed" character has evolved. She said,

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:01.140
"Something that feels exciting is&nbsp;
that I've always been invited to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.398
be kind of a co-author and figure&nbsp;
that out with the collaborators."

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:08.040
While speaking with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;
Tessa Thompson opened up about the importance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.900
of maintaining Bianca's character arc throughout&nbsp;
the franchise. In "Creed III," Bianca and Adonis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.820
are living the good life, enjoying their success&nbsp;
and fame. Because life is so cozy in Los Angeles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.560
a part of Bianca, namely her affinity for&nbsp;
Philadelphia, is less visible onscreen.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.120
In the first "Creed," Bianca and Adonis first&nbsp;
begin to fall in love over cheesesteaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.160
a Philadelphia staple. On their date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.780
Bianca explains to Adonis the meaning behind&nbsp;
"jawn," which has strong Philadelphia roots.

00:01:34.055 --> 00:01:35.015
"So what's a jawn?"

00:01:35.015 --> 00:01:40.860
"It's a noun. See, these is jawns, this is a jawn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.440
this restaurant that we're&nbsp;
in is a jawn, you're a jawn."

00:01:43.879 --> 00:01:48.000
While the scene doesn't have the momentum or&nbsp;
high stakes of Adonis training or fighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.280
it does allow Bianca and the boxer to bond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.205
eventually leading to their relationship,&nbsp;
which is at the heart of "Creed III."

00:01:54.205 --> 00:01:59.880
Because "jawn" is so uniquely Philly, Thompson&nbsp;
refused to use it in the LA-focused "Creed III."

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.300
"I said to them, 'I'm not saying 'jawn'&nbsp;
in this movie because we've heard it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.701
we've done it. I want to break new territory.'&nbsp;
Not saying 'jawn' was also a way of saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:11.880
inside of the filmmaking that you are going to&nbsp;
witness someone that is constantly evolving."

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.320
Bianca's evolution from up-and-coming&nbsp;
musician to rockstar to talented producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.400
has been a powerful emotional arc of the&nbsp;
Creed trilogy, and subtly acknowledging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.240
how far she's come from the Philly musician&nbsp;
we met in the first film is an interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.320
and daring route for the character. And&nbsp;
Thompson doing her best to make Bianca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.700
feel like a real person is nothing new for the&nbsp;
actress. In a 2015 interview with The Source,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.267
Thompson revealed that she had never been to&nbsp;
Philadelphia prior to the first film's production.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:40.020
"I never stepped foot in Philly&nbsp;
before I flew here to make the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.360
and I spent about two months&nbsp;
before shooting just getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.701
integrated and learning the dialect&nbsp;
and hanging out in the musical scene."

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:49.260
In a separate interview with The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, Thompson opened up about how she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.980
spent hours with Philly natives to learn&nbsp;
the vernacular that persisted throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.362
the city. Years later, it's interesting to see&nbsp;
how invested Thompson is with the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.362 --> 00:03:01.200
to the point that she refuses to use a word&nbsp;
that's so synonymous with Philly culture now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.460
that it's no longer applicable. As Bianca&nbsp;
becomes more attached to Los Angeles, is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.000
it possible that she's becoming more personal to&nbsp;
Thompson, who was born in California metropolis?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.954
With "Creed III," the future&nbsp;
of the franchise is open ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.954 --> 00:03:17.327
so here's hoping we get more of Bianca and&nbsp;
Creed as they tackle their next major battle.

